  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Consider the function \(f(x) = \frac{6}{x-2}\).</para>
      <para id="para-00002">To find out the sets of possible input and output values of the function, Clare created a table and evaluated \(f\) at some values of \(x\). Along the way, she ran into some trouble.</para>
           <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001"> <para id="para-00003">Find \(f(x)\) for each \(x\)-value Clare listed. Describe what Clare’s trouble might be.</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00001">
        <tgroup cols="6"><tbody><row>
            <entry>
             <emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry>
       -10
      </entry>
            <entry>
        0
      </entry>
            <entry>
        \(\frac12\)
      </entry>
            <entry>
      2
      </entry>
            <entry>
        8
      </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry>
             <emphasis>\(f(x)\)</emphasis>
            </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
            <entry> </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
   </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          
          <para id="para-00004">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00005">When \(x\) is \(2\), \(f(x)\) is \(\frac60\), which is undefined.</para>
          <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00002">
            <tgroup cols="6"><tbody><row>
                <entry>
                 <emphasis>\(x\)</emphasis>
                </entry>
                <entry>
           -10
          </entry>
                <entry>
            0
          </entry>
                <entry>
            \(\frac12\)
          </entry>
                <entry>
          2
          </entry>
                <entry>
            8
          </entry>
              </row>
              <row>
                <entry>
                 <emphasis>\(f(x)\)</emphasis>
                </entry>
                <entry>-\(\frac12\)</entry>
                <entry>-3</entry>
                <entry>-4</entry>
                <entry>\(\frac60\)</entry>
                <entry>1</entry>
              </row>
            </tbody></tgroup></table>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>Use graphing technology to graph function \(f\). What do you notice about the graph?
 </item>
      </list>
      <media alt=""><iframe src="../../media/desmos/a47b5bb4ba783be55a7067b919f165f14dcc36ce.html" width="500" height="400"/></media><!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      
